{"kind":"finding","id":"F-trajectory-orbit-012-01","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/TrajectorySidecarBinaryTests.cs","line":814,"method":"TrackSection_BoundarySeamFlag_PreservesCurrentBinaryValue","category":"T3","severity":"Low","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/TrajectorySidecarBinary.cs:855; swap the isBoundarySeam read with the adjacent field read so the positional decode desyncs -> red on the AssertPointEqual frame check","what_it_asserts":"a current-version write/read preserves isBoundarySeam true and the section frame payload","why_weak":"the block comment claims it reads a v7 legacy file and expects isBoundarySeam == false; the code writes at CurrentRecordingFormatVersion with the flag true, so the documented legacy-read contract is untested and a reader regression on old files would look covered","proposed_action":"rewrite the comment to describe the current-version positional-integrity contract it actually pins, and either add a real hand-written legacy-version fixture or state that pre-bump sidecars are rejected by IsRecordingSchemaCompatible and need no read path","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"F-trajectory-orbit-012-02","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/TrajectorySidecarBinaryTests.cs","line":756,"method":"TrackSection_BoundarySeamFlag_RoundTripsThroughBinaryCodec","category":"T2","severity":"Low","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/TrajectorySidecarBinary.cs:830; write a constant false instead of track.isBoundarySeam -> this test and its twin at line 814 go red together","what_it_asserts":"a seam-flagged TrackSection survives a current-version binary write/read","why_weak":"the twin at line 814 writes the same current-version seam-true section and makes the same two assertions plus stronger frame checks; the stale v8/v9 comments here describe versions the fixture does not construct","proposed_action":"merge the two into one seam round-trip test that keeps the richer frame assertions, or give this one a genuinely distinct payload shape (e.g. a seam section alongside a non-seam section to prove per-section fidelity)","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
